# Test: a DISABLED mcp block with a portless server entry starts nothing
# VALIDATES: the `enabled` gate. ExtractMCPConfig returns ok=false for a block
# the operator switched off, whatever its server entries say, so the port default
# reaches only the blocks that asked for a listener.
# PREVENTS: an upgrade starting MCP on 127.0.0.1:8080 for a deployment that never
# enabled it. The default is applied inside the gate, never before it.
#
# `enabled` is OMITTED rather than written false: the YANG default is false, so
# the omitted leaf is the shape an operator actually leaves behind, and it is the
# one a naive tree walk is most likely to mis-read.
stdin=config:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp {
	router-id 10.0.0.1;
	session { asn { local 65533; } }
}
environment {
	mcp {
		server alt {
			ip 127.0.0.1;
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=config
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=configuration valid
